Z||000007||ChadMan||09-20-2001||06:06 PM||||Sorry, Wolfhound, I've heard too much talk from the political left this week about how our backing of Israel got us into this mess, how we are such an "arrogant" nation that we deserve what happened on 9/11, how sending troops to capture and/or kill the people responsible is "futile" and will be "another Vietnam," etc.<P>If you fought in Vietnam, saw the pointlessness of that conflict, and hoped to help VVWA to improve matters for returning veterans and to pressure our government to either fully back a winning effort or get the hell out of Vietnam, I respect that.<P>But when I see that peace rallies are already springing up in the SF Bay area when they haven't even pulled all the bodies out from under the WTC, well...it just gets me a little hot.  This is not Vietnam, or Haiti, or Somalia.  <P>And I don't care if this makes me a bigot, or a racist, or any other label lefties like to throw around:  the life of one American soldier (or dead Manhattan office worker) means more to me than all the goat herders in Afghanistan.  Not because Afghan lives aren't precious, but because the lives of my countrymen are far more precious.<P>We've got a crazy lefty girl at work organizing people to go eat at a Middle Eastern restaurant next week and calling it "progressive social action."  Well, Jesus Christ.  I think I'll organize people to go eat cheeseburgers in support of America.<P>||||reg||4
